{"reply":"What seems to connect the scene and your billing mistake is not simply “an error happened,” but the pressure to make the error disappear before it becomes a social event. In the chapter, the gardeners repaint the roses before the Queen sees them; in your note, you fixed the mistake and then told yourself it was “already handled.” That parallel doesn’t prove the same motive, but it offers a gentle question: was silence protecting you from a feared reaction—anger, embarrassment, being seen as incompetent, extra work, or having to explain yourself?

Research gives that question some context. A 2023 study of nurses found that willingness to report errors was shaped by psychological safety, leader inclusiveness, and safety climate; it also describes error reporting as carrying real or perceived interpersonal risk. The study is specific to healthcare teams, so it cannot explain your situation by itself, but it supports the idea that people’s silence is often influenced by what they expect will happen socially, not just by whether the practical problem has been fixed. [Read the study here](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10599306/).

So your reaction might be worth holding in two parts: fixing the mistake may have been responsible and effective, while not disclosing it may still reveal something about how safe it felt to be seen making it. If you imagine telling the relevant person now, what is the first consequence you picture—not the consequence you think is objectively likely, but the one your body or imagination seems to prepare for?","evidence_uses":[{"source_kind":"book_corpus","evidence_id":"pg11-v01b38ea4-ch08-ln1931-1970","source_location":"Chapter 8 — The Queen’s Croquet-Ground, source lines 1931-1970","exact_quote":null},{"source_kind":"memory","evidence_id":"mem_e6f7d4401e78a703d2c7e3350b8384e8764d87919bab8fd773e14400caee081d","exact_quote":null},{"source_kind":"web","evidence_id":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10599306/","exact_quote":null}],"memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}

